# AI use disclosure

## Tools and contribution

OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex was used during development to generate and revise substantial portions of the HTML, CSS and JavaScript; procedural illustrations and directional animations; interface layout; synthesized sound-effect code; educational descriptions; English/Spanish localization; documentation; and verification scripts. The project creator supplied the game concept, requested mechanics, artistic direction, feedback and revision decisions. This is an AI-assisted project, not a claim of entirely hand-written code or hand-drawn artwork.

The visible illustrations are rendered by Canvas/SVG code created with AI assistance. No downloaded NASA photographs, generated-video files or recorded music are bundled. Visible in-game labels identify AI-generated code-drawn artwork, and Voyager's exported memory images include the same label. Audio effects are synthesized at runtime by AI-assisted Web Audio code; no standalone generated audio files are bundled.

NASA/JPL pages and Horizons are the sources of mission history and numerical data. AI helped compile and explain those references; it is not the scientific authority or the origin of the underlying NASA/JPL measurements. See SOURCES.md and SCIENCE_REVIEW.md. Font authors and licenses are listed separately in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

## Dates

The creator reports development on November 14–15, 2026. This is a creator-provided date statement, not an independent certification of the development period or event eligibility. The official 2026 event page lists November 14–15. Code and content continue to receive the revisions documented in source versions.

